## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical performance optimization skills and understanding of modern frontend tooling. Companies need engineers who can deliver fast, scalable user experiences and systematically improve application metrics.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates will mention: 1) Bundle analysis to identify largest chunks, 2) Code splitting strategies (route-based vs component-based), 3) Tree shaking configuration, 4) Dynamic imports for non-critical features, 5) Image optimization and lazy loading, 6) Service worker caching strategy.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Route-based code splitting
const Dashboard = React.lazy(() => import('./Dashboard'));
const Analytics = React.lazy(() => import('./Analytics'));

// Component-based splitting with error boundaries
const HeavyChart = React.lazy(() => import('./HeavyChart'));

function App() {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<LoadingSpinner />}>
      <Routes>
        <Route path="/dashboard" element={<Dashboard />} />
        <Route path="/analytics" element={<Analytics />} />
      </Routes>
    </Suspense>
  );
}
```

